<h2 id="the-problem-it-solves">The problem it solves</h2><p>Young innovators often keep their best ideas to themselves because they fear someone more powerful will take them. That fear is reasonable, and it is costly: ideas that are never shared are never improved, tested or adopted. The Idea Ledger is designed to make sharing safe.</p>
<h2 id="what-happens-when-you-submit">What happens when you submit</h2><p>When you send an idea through the portal, three things are recorded at once. The idea gets a permanent <b>ID</b>. The server records a <b>timestamp</b> in universal time. And the text of your idea is passed through <b>SHA-256</b>, a standard cryptographic function that turns any text into a 64-character fingerprint. You receive all three in a receipt.</p>
<blockquote>Change a single letter of your idea and its fingerprint changes completely. That is what makes it proof.</blockquote>
<h2 id="what-is-public-and-what-is-not">What is public, and what is not</h2><p>The public ledger shows only the ID, the date, the title, the fingerprint and the stage your idea has reached. The full text stays private unless you choose to share it. Later, anyone can take the exact text you hold, compute its fingerprint, and confirm that it matches the ledger entry from that date. You can try it yourself on the Idea Portal page.</p>
<h2 id="what-it-is-not">What it is not</h2><p>The ledger is proof of priority, not a patent. It does not stop someone from using a similar idea, but it gives you a clear, verifiable record that you had it first, which matters for credit, for partnerships and, if you choose to file one, for a patent application.</p><p class="tags"><a class="tg" href="{{ route('insights.index') }}?tag=idea-ledger">#idea-ledger</a><a class="tg" href="{{ route('insights.index') }}?tag=sha-256">#sha-256</a><a class="tg" href="{{ route('insights.index') }}?tag=protection">#protection</a></p></article></div></section>
